WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.840
In an attempt to finally get rid of SCP-682,
the Hard to Destroy Reptile, the SCP Foundation

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:11.200
considered leaving it inside SCP-3008, the
Infinite IKEA, and just letting it be their

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.620
problem for a change.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.090
How do you think it worked out?

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:19.519
The Foundation sealed 682 into a box and sent
it inside of 3008 with an unmanned drone.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:23.880
There was no response for 24 hours, at which
point, eighteen instances of the malformed

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:29.089
IKEA staff exited the building, each one carrying
a large box stamped with the IKEA logo.

00:00:29.089 --> 00:00:32.169
They set these on the ground and then headed
back inside.

00:00:32.169 --> 00:00:36.649
Inside of each of these boxes was a living
part of SCP-682, and like all things that

00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:41.270
come out of an IKEA box, 682 had trouble correctly
putting itself back together.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:46.530
Thankfully, this granted the Foundation time
to reestablish containment before SCP-682

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.639
had the chance to properly regenerate.

